{
  "_comment": [
    "The fixed question set. Changing it invalidates comparison with stored",
    "results, so add questions rather than editing them, and note it in the",
    "learning note when the set changes.",
    "",
    "`expected_documents` names the source a correct answer must come from \u2014",
    "not the wording of the answer. Grading against expected text would need a",
    "second model to judge it, and would move with the chat model rather than",
    "with retrieval, which is the thing being measured.",
    "",
    "`expected_phrases` is optional and only used with --with-answers. It is a",
    "crude substring check on purpose: it catches an answer that lost the",
    "specific fact, without pretending to grade prose.",
    "",
    "An empty `expected_documents` means nothing in the corpus answers this.",
    "The right behaviour is to retrieve weakly and say so, and those cases are",
    "scored separately as `unanswerable`."
  ],
